#============
# Virtualenv
#============
# Identify a venv by its marker files, not by directory name. Bare names like [Bb]in and
# [Ll]ib have no slash, so git matches them at any depth in EVERY repository -- this file
# is the global excludesfile, so they silently ignored bin/, lib/, include/, local/ and
# Scripts/ project-wide. New files under a tracked bin/ would not stage without -f.
.Python
.venv/
venv/
pip-selfcheck.json
pyvenv.cfg
